-- 0150: the aṣl of the 13 Ghāfir 40:1–3 roots — ONE row per book, each in that book's own words and read by its own
-- method (Ibn Fāris «أصل صحيح يدل على», al-Rāghib «في الأصل», al-Khalīl / al-Jawharī / Lisān / Tāj / al-Qāmūs / al-Miṣbāḥ
-- their head sense, Ibn Durayd his first sense, Lane in ENGLISH: "primary signification", "properly", "originally", A1),
-- with block id + page for the backlink. Exactly ONE primary per root, chosen by what most books share (never Ibn Fāris
-- by default): كتب Ibn Durayd, علم al-Khalīl, ذنب al-Rāghib, قبل al-Jawharī, نزل al-Rāghib, غفر al-Khalīl, توب Lisān;
-- Ibn Fāris where his statement is the majority reading and covers a branch others leave unexplained (عزز شدد عقب طول اله صير).
-- Fixed: نزل had five primaries; rows that quoted how a WORD is formed, not what the root means (طول/اله Ṣiḥāḥ, اله Mufradāt);
-- cut-off or mis-mined rows (نزل/كتب/قبل Mufradāt, غفر Ṣiḥāḥ, نزل Lisān mid-entry); narrows_id links with no basis cleared.
-- Corpus gaps noted per root (al-Asās mostly not ingested; Jamhara and some al-Qāmūs / al-Miṣbāḥ entries filed under other keys).
ALTER TABLE ar_ling_root_asl ADD COLUMN block_id TEXT;
